{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SSJPq7QvwEkKYYppd9ps9j","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Discovery Quality & Surfacing â€” Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 5 wave(s) planned\n4\t(W1 felt briefing vertical; W2 ingest + backfills + serving trust; W3 digest + notability;\n5\tW4 taste score; W5 close the loop).\n6\t\n7\t## Waves\n8\t\n9\t### Wave 5 â€” Close the loop â€” âœ… GREEN (2026-06-10)\n10\t\n11\t- **Status:** converged after 1 fix-iteration (1 MAJOR); committed. Code complete; the server.py change\n12\t  needs the batched plugin rebuild + John's manual reinstall + smoke (shared with W2).\n13\t- **Files:** `helping-hand-plugin/mcp-servers/aurora-kb/server.py` (`_compute_matches` usage modifier),\n14\t  `morning_briefing.py` (`_top_finds` usage modifier on top of interest_score), `bin/weekly_digest.py`\n15\t  (value section), `bin/retirement_policy.py` (new â€” nightly, audited, reversible), `bin/run-morning-briefing.cmd`\n16\t  (retirement wired in), `tests/test_wave5_close_loop.py` (new).\n17\t- **Usage modifier:** `0.10 * tanh(net/3.0)` where `net = Î£ Â±0.5^(age_days/30)` â€” hard-bounded to the\n18\t  CLOSED interval [-0.10, +0.10] (saturates to the cap; proven under 1e9 loads), exponential 30-day\n19\t  half-life. Applied in HH `_compute_matches` AND top_finds/digest ranking; near-ties reorder, a >0.20\n20\t  base gap is never overcome (no runaway); zero-usage order byte-identical to pre-W5; read-only briefing\n21\t  reads telemetry, never writes; server path fails open.\n22\t- **Retirement policy** (reversible, retired_at-only, never DELETE; --dry-run + --audit-out; owns the\n23\t  library filesystem): (a) N=2 stale over â‰¥2 DISTINCT probe-days â†’ retire; (b) never-surfaced AND\n24\t  interest_score < AURORA_RETIRE_MIN_INTEREST (0.3) AND older than AURORA_RETIRE_AGE_DAYS (60) â†’ retire.\n25\t  Wired into `run-morning-briefing.cmd` (not a new task â€” task reg needs elevation).\n26\t- **EXECUTE â†’ gate (1026) â†’ 2 reviewers (A GO; B GO+1 MAJOR) â†’ fix iter 1 â†’ re-gate (1029) â†’ re-review GO.**\n27\t- **MAJOR fixed (the key catch):** the stale rule originally used the top-2 link_health rows by\n28\t  timestamp with no inter-probe-day gate, so the W3 activation's same-day probes would have retired\n29\t  **7 live artifacts tonight** â€” contradicting the spec's \"armed, not demonstrated (~2 weeks of probe\n30\t  history)\". Fixed: require 2 DISTINCT stale probe-days. **Independently verified on the LIVE KB\n31\t  (read-only): stale_candidates 7â†’0, cold_candidates 0, local skills 822-824 protected â€” nothing\n32\t  retires tonight.** New tests lock the masked same-day case.\n33\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` â†’ 1029 passed (was 1009; +20). No live retirement run. KB backups retained.\n34\t\n35\t### Wave 4 â€” The taste score â€” âœ… GREEN (2026-06-10)\n36\t\n37\t- **Status:** converged with 0 fix-iterations (both reviewers GO; only non-blocking MINORs); committed.\n38\t  Live activation done (migration applied + supervised LLM run).\n39\t- **Files:** `roles/taste.py` (new â€” `resolve_taste_model`, `score_one`, `heuristic_score`, `run` nightly\n40\t  leg + cap + degrade-to-heuristic, `ensure_scored`/`score_pending` on-demand), `kb/migrations/0025_interest_score.sql`\n41\t  (+ `kb/schema.sql` mirror: `interest_score REAL`, `interest_why TEXT`, `interest_scored_at TEXT`),\n42\t  `kb/pricing.yaml` (`default_models.taste` â†’ `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`, already priced $1/$5 verified),\n43\t  `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md` (new â€” John-editable taste profile), `morning_briefing.py` (`_top_finds`\n44\t  orders by interest_score, NULL-last, W1 tiebreak; why upgrades to interest_why), `tests/test_taste.py`\n45\t  + `tests/test_pricing_keys.py` (E17 priced-tag identity).\n46\t- **Model:** `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` â€” already priced, cheapest Anthropic tier, no new provider dep.\n47\t- **EXECUTE â†’ gate (1009) â†’ 2 reviewers